Hi Laura,

Thank you for reading both explanations with me yesterday. I will keep the audience and English wording as reviewed in the two v0.3 PDFs we shared on 22 May: the ten reception points for checking, possible resending and enquiries, and the six administrator points for investigation and handover. In particular, “received” does not mean that the business process is complete, and reception staff are not being asked to investigate logs.

I have attached both PDFs so we have the same versions for the record. Our review did not establish R7 behaviour or decide the reception method. The behaviour still needs to be checked against the system, and the publication decision and date remain open.

Thank you again for helping us make the boundary clearer.

Best,
Miyu

